# Modules: the export variable, .l of modules, host functions in modules and qualified names a.b. Generated by conformance/tools/gen_modules.py: edit the generator, not this file.
# docs/design-principles.md decides every open question; a `why` line names the principle.
#
# Tags: qualified = a.b on dictionaries (reading, writing, calling); modules = the export variable and .l of a module file
# (a case writes its module files with .oc .tc .p .cc and deletes them with .df, hence strings dicts sysio).
# Macros in the comments: {P} is the absolute path, {R} the ./ path, {U} the ../tmp/ path and {B} the bare name (found beside the importing file) of the case's own files.
# The runner substitutes a temporary directory for /tmp in the absolute fixture paths and removes it after each case.
# Error kinds: a missing key is `name`; a base that is not a dictionary, writing to a read-only dictionary and every wrong argument of .l or .extern are `type`;
# every failure of the module graph (missing file, cycle, a bare name that no directory of the search order has) is `system`.

@ modules.read strings dicts qualified
# d.a is d@"a"
> d:::{;"a";1}
> d.a
= 1

@ modules.read-nested strings dicts qualified
> d:::{;"a";:{;"b";2}}
> d.a.b
= 2

@ modules.read-three-deep strings dicts qualified
> d:::{;"a";:{;"b";:{;"c";3}}}
> d.a.b.c
= 3

@ modules.read-in-expression strings dicts qualified
> d:::{;"a";4}
> (d.a*2)+d.a
= 12

@ modules.read-then-index strings dicts qualified
# d.l@1 is (d.l)@1: the name is d.l
> d:::{;"l";[10 20 30]}
> d.l@1
= 20

@ modules.read-under-monads strings dicts qualified
> d:::{;"l";[10 20 30]}
> (#d.l),*d.l
= [3 10]

@ modules.read-letters-and-digits strings dicts qualified
> d:::{;"a1";3}
> d.a1
= 3

@ modules.read-float-entry strings dicts qualified float
> d:::{;"a";1.5}
> d.a+2.5
= 4.0

